>Excuse me?  I didn't think the plus on a piece of armor could safely get
>that large.  Are you sure?  If anyone does know, could you please tell me
>how high I can safely enchant a piece of armor.  (I'm playing NH 3.1.3)

Spoilers, obviously.


Some armor and weapons will vibrate when they've been enchanted to 
full.  Don't enchant them again.  Some will not, and will just blow
up on your next attempt without warning.  Oops.  You may assume
that if a type of armor or weapon that is known to vibrate has not
done so, it is safe to keep enchanting it.  I don't know if this 
is perfectly safe in practice, but it works for me.

From my experience, +3 armor may safely be enchanted.  +4 or better
has a shot of blowing up.

Also, +5 weapons may safely be enchanted.  +6 or better is risky.

There may be some armor or weapons to which these rules don't apply.
I don't know, because I'm not in the mood for source-sifting right
now.  And this thread was just around a month ago.  

Bless your enchantment scrolls before enchanting +3 armor or +5
weapons.  Use the uncursed models on +2 armor and +4 weapons to
get to these jumping-off points into the nearly-unsafe.  All this
assumes a surplus of scrolls.  

